% divergence: bitshift-zero-fill
% expect-output: 33554426
% expect-output: 2147483647
% expect-output: -1416
% Scenario: a negative integer shifted right. `bitshift` moves zeros
% into the vacated high bits of the 32-bit pattern, as the operator's
% description prescribes (PLRM3 section 8.2, bitshift), so -663 shifted
% right by 7 is 2^25 - 6; other interpreters sign-extend and give -6.
% Left shifts of a negative are the same in both.
-663 -7 bitshift =
-1 -1 bitshift =
-708 1 bitshift =
